 "notes": [
  "PROPOSED by Kernel K6, Lantern Quay Hamlet, under the 5 m grid rule (10 Nov late note).",
  "As your review asked, the quay row moves down to the real shore: the beach strip at the foot of the sea escarpment, about 280 m south-south-west of the K1 site point.",
  "The escarpment (25-40 m) is climbed by a stair (a piece, not a graded street). Above it the hamlet sits on five contour terraces 8 m apart (58, 66, 74, 82 and 90 m), one row each, one level per segment; the terraces stop short of the escarpment so the ground between them and the quay can be graded.",
  "The stepped main street and the side stairs between terraces are stair pieces (listed below with their ends and levels), not graded streets. Boats and air only, so no vehicle road is needed.",
  "Lamps are yours.",
  "Stairs, not graded streets (a climb of 8 m between terraces 35 m apart is steeper than the 31 degree bank can grade; the hamlet is foot-only): stair lane 1 (58 to 66 m): from (7276, 16549) at 58 m to (7290, 16586) at 66 m; stair lane 1 (66 to 74 m): from (7290, 16586) at 66 m to (7307, 16631) at 74 m; stepped main street (stairs) (66 to 74 m): from (7377, 16514) at 66 m to (7393, 16556) at 74 m; stepped main street (stairs) (74 to 82 m): from (7393, 16556) at 74 m to (7410, 16600) at 82 m; stepped main street (stairs) (82 to 90 m): from (7410, 16600) at 82 m to (7434, 16666) at 90 m",
